<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lal Kot</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lal Kot is the earliest identifiable fortified city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, a citadel in the south of the modern city whose building is attributed to the Tomara king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anangapala-ii">Anangapala II</a> in the 11th century. The Chahamana ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithviraj-chauhan">Prithviraj Chauhan</a> extended it as Qila Rai Pithora in the 12th century, and after the Ghurid conquest of 1192 it became the core of the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> city, around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutb-minar">Qutb Minar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lal-kot.jpg" alt="Lal Kot" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roboture · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Outer_Wall_of_Lal_kot_and_Rai_Pithora.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
